WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 8.4 · Marketing & Communications
Storytelling and ethical storytelling

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Tell true stories with people, not about them, and record their consent.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Get informed consent and explain uses, time and withdrawal.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Let people use their own words and approve the result.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Take extra care with children; when in doubt, don’t publish.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Tide Line Youth Collective (Community group · idea stage, Indonesia)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Parent consent plus the young person’s own yes on the day. No names, uniforms or deep water. Young people write their captions.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You write your storytelling rules and set up a consent log.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
